{"name":"Gotta Have It","hex":"#d0c2b4","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gotta","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Synonym of have got to, have to"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Contraction of got +‎ a."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gotta"},{"term":"have","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To possess, own.","To hold, as something at someone's disposal."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A wealthy or privileged person.","One who has some (contextually specified) thing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/have"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pepsi","blocks":[{"text":"Pepsi is a carbonated soft drink with a cola flavor, the flagship product of PepsiCo. In 2023, Pepsi was the second most valuable soft drink brand worldwide behind Coca-Cola; the two share a long-standing rivalry in what has been called the \"cola wars\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pepsi","wikidata":"Q47719"},{"title":"Gotta Have It (Jay-Z and Kanye West song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Gotta Have It\" is a song by American rappers Kanye West and Jay-Z from their collaborative album, Watch the Throne (2011). The song was produced by West and the Neptunes, and samples three original compositions by James Brown: \"Don't Tell a Lie About Me and I Won't Tell the Truth About You\", \"People Get Up and Drive Your Funky Soul\" and \"My Thang\". The song explores themes of wealth, decadence and the economic stature in the US. The song received positive reviews from critics who complimented the production and the clever wordplay of the two rappers."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gotta_Have_It_(Jay-Z_and_Kanye_West_song)","wikidata":"Q5587986"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Pepsi_355_ml%2C_591_ml%2C_and_710_ml%2C_Canada_%28obverse%29%2C_2026-03-05.jpg/500px-Pepsi_355_ml%2C_591_ml%2C_and_710_ml%2C_Canada_%28obverse%29%2C_2026-03-05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaig